course: dictionary
lesson: 7095
title: Peacefully: calm, quiet, and without fighting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Peacefully is an adverb. It tells you how something is done, so it describes an action. It means in a calm, quiet way, or without fighting or violence. You can hear the word peace inside it, and peace is the same idea.
explain: «Across the road there may be a counter-protest, and both sides are allowed to protest peacefully.» The sentence does not say the protests are loud or angry. The word peacefully tells you how they protest: with no fighting. Ask yourself, "How is this being done?" Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Sometimes a word is used gently to soften a hard idea. «Passed away peacefully» is a kind way to say that someone died without pain or struggle. A word like this, used instead of a harder one, is called a euphemism.
fact: Peacefully means in a calm, quiet way, or without fighting or violence.
fact: Peacefully is an adverb, so it tells you how an action happens.
fact: «Peacefully» can be used to describe a calm, quiet scene, such as a sleeping child or a quiet afternoon.
fact: «Died peacefully» means died without pain or struggle. It is a gentle way to talk about a sad thing.
fact: A euphemism is a softer word used in place of a harder one, especially when the truth is sad.
exercise: «Both sides are allowed to protest peacefully.» What does peacefully mean here? | *Without fighting or violence | Very loudly and angrily | Quickly, before anyone can stop them | Only in the dark
exercise: «The children sat peacefully by the lake, watching the ducks.» What does peacefully suggest? | *In a calm, quiet way | Angrily | Noisily | In a hurry
exercise: Peacefully is which part of speech? | Verb | *Adverb | Noun | Adjective
test: «Striking workers stood outside, peacefully asking others not to go in.» Which word tells you how the workers asked? | Striking | Workers | Outside | *Peacefully
test: Ellie says, «Grandad passed away peacefully.» What does peacefully tell you? | He woke up and went out | He was very angry at the doctors | *He died without pain or struggle | He was in pain and struggling
exam: Which sentence uses peacefully correctly? | The crowd threw bottles and shouted peacefully | The peacefully big dog barked at the postman | Peacefully is the name of the football team | *They solved the argument peacefully, by talking it through
